^  [LINK: (a) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_H._Beyer#cite_ref-ANobit_2-0]   [LINK: (b) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_H._Beyer#cite_ref-ANobit_2-1]  Roche, Daniel Jonas. "The Architect's Newspaper",  [LINK: (The Architect's Newspaper) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Architect%27s_Newspaper] , January 23, 2026. Accessed January 28, 2026. "In 1954, he graduated with an undergraduate art degree from Denison University in Ohio, where he studied sculpture and music. He then enrolled at Harvard GSD where he earned his Bachelor and Master of Architecture."

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_H._Beyer#cite_ref-3]  Koster, John. "N.Y. architect hired to renovate library",  [LINK: (The Record) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Record_(North_Jersey)] , August 11, 1978. Accessed January 28, 2026, via  [LINK: (Newspapers.com) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newspapers.com] . "The township council last night hired New York architect John H. Beyer to remodel the town's 57-year-old library. Beyer, of the firm of Beyer, Blinder & Belle, has two weeks to submit a detailed plan with cost estimates.... Beyer told the council he would have no trouble staying within the confines of an $837,000 federal grant in remodeling the library, whose 16,500 square feet of space have grown cramped."

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_H._Beyer#cite_ref-4]  Dunlap, David W. "Grand Central Makeover Is Readied",  [LINK: (The New York Times) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times] , January 29, 1995. Accessed January 28, 2026. "The plan has been drawn up by Beyer Blinder Belle, which last month won the architecture firm award from the American Institute of Architects for its overall body of work, "incorporating vital new uses for our landmark structures." The partner in charge of Grand Central is John Belle. The total project cost is $113.8 million, of which $71.7 million goes to construction and $25.9 million goes to architectural, engineering, management, leasing, financing and legal fees, marketing and promotion, retail tenant allowances and insurance."

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_H._Beyer#cite_ref-5]  "John H. Beyer Married in Ohio",  [LINK: (The Record) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Record_(North_Jersey)] , December 22, 1958. Accessed January 28, 2026, via  [LINK: (Newspapers.com) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newspapers.com] . "Miss Virginia Van Horn, daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Donald G. Van Horn of Monroeville, Ohio, was married to John Henry Beyer, son of Mr. and Mrs. Henry Kraft Beyer of 68 Church Street here, Saturday at 4:30 P. M. in St. Peter's Episcopal Church, Lakewood, Ohio."

